  "proof_file_sha256": "7b0aa8904b1b0d130e77f6815bfd7950addabc959b4a75e5d084c6660f0de50f",
  "claims_reviewed": [
    {
      "id": "GMR1",
      "block_sha256": "264b43b07034fb23d413f32547ae31406a6c0cc9792a6440afd8c52e39d59d9d",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The standard character uses the rational negative-part formula and adelic trace. The local-character parameter and diagonal annihilator argument preserve every original IsCharAF character and yield one standard character before tuple choices."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR2",
      "block_sha256": "95da7e201d09bfc9b2a3a17d1ecbb42f349e71f54ead54ae8db3a0979cf01564",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The Fourier-inversion predicate is the literal source SelfDual predicate. Nondegeneracy includes split quadratic algebras; scaling is fixed by the square of the Haar factor. Compactly supported smooth/locally constant tests justify uniqueness and rank-zero normalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR3",
      "block_sha256": "b21327fc6682db2e3693f855c84fd0d6d68ca312e06786cbb33df2d5aa055879",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The derivative X*JY+Y*JX is onto because X*J has a right inverse; division by two occurs in characteristic-zero local fields. The argument covers singular Gram parameters and primes above two."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR4",
      "block_sha256": "b7f59b36cd6962b59ef0ed900da317dc256383057efe89444df0054e2b41c937",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Local analytic charts and their vertical Jacobians glue for every fixed additive Haar pair. The compact support is contained in the independent open locus; finite subordinate charts prove continuity at every parameter without asserting ambient finiteness near dependent singular tuples."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR5",
      "block_sha256": "b17fb4a2a8eb36b03d34d0f5834e30dd6548c94a7788f7d1141d2942b952261b",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Continuous fiber integrals upgrade almost-everywhere equality to pointwise equality. Local finiteness on the independent fiber and Radon regularity identify measures. The determinant ratio in covariance has the correct numerator for the target map, and unitary/unipotent cases have ratio one."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR6",
      "block_sha256": "43b13758c14fd95f2827718e10557213c6e1a135b9347b34ca9a547c4e9c2e92",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The inert frame orbit count follows from the norm character sum and the unitary group order; the split count is the GL quotient. The exact normalized product supplies FFCount uniformly in its original range, including a=0."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR7",
      "block_sha256": "e124fafe1176d3db5f8be37bcc9bc7e09704ba8e7868f8bd0e022c2b86d36b86",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "At the finite exceptional complement both source trace lattices are self-dual of mass one. Smooth residue lifting gives N_m=N_1 q^(d(m-1)); averaging over shrinking Hermitian balls and a cutoff supported in the independent locus gives the exact canonical fiber mass for any allowed rational basis."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR8",
      "block_sha256": "68a4694498ba55b9cd8270a842da665e76c9ae6090b59a7cd752fc5c6efbeddc",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The product is shown strictly positive through the absolutely summable logarithms, with exponent n-a+1 at least three. Convergence is not silently substituted for nonvanishing."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR9",
      "block_sha256": "ffd41fac74b4800bd4520edcff310fbcb1503ecd02fb41325e431ca5005d1bb6",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The normalized compact fiber probability products glue, then one explicit convergent scalar restores the original local masses. Every original pure finite factorization has compact support in one restricted-product chart. AllSome includes both existence and every permitted self-dual/fiber witness, supplied by uniqueness."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR10",
      "block_sha256": "709fc7417f8720ea407ccdcf94dd4cf5a3e740a2481e113da697caa24a20770c",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The local isometry extension is written for both nondegenerate and degenerate subspaces and the split algebra. Integral smooth lifting at almost all places produces an actual adelic group element. Skew-adjoint tangent extension gives local sections and the actual quotient topology."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR11",
      "block_sha256": "03272dc9ddd48c90cfa56190d8a541d0629c0a6ce627ce0202465aa178f2208b",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The quotient integral starts from an arbitrary stabilizer Haar and determines its unique positive scalar relative to the supplied ambient Haar. Independence of the inner integral from representatives proves the original every-section formula even for nonmeasurable sections."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR12",
      "block_sha256": "e6decf1a0b6b912cb9510136f9f3318a70685d78b0054e18bfb92bb674bf3868",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full original global stabilizer-measure supplier is obtained at every IsCharAF, tuple, Hermitian witness and Haar normalization in its stated range. Original volume premises remain printed but the direct construction does not invoke their arithmetic theta identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR13",
      "block_sha256": "7054ac9c661ca509476aa68aecdb0c58dda4e87f6a9d48f483bd78132dcd7990",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The singular independent frame fiber is the actual orbit. The strengthened paragraph covers every supplied additive Haar pair and every original fiber family through pointwise uniqueness, so the full intermediate compatible-fiber source theorem retains its broader scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR14",
      "block_sha256": "c32156ae36460f1c43a7e76cb8c08bd11166db084b2290f5a0c2091c4685454f",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The nondegenerate trace pairing on the unitary Lie algebra and its invariance give absolute adjoint determinant one. The analytic Haar-density argument proves unimodularity for every supplied local normalization, including the split group."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR15",
      "block_sha256": "d73771507f530046feb61238d5018b7b35c979d3e19fa1098489162ec9887bcf",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The flag action on the fiber is right upper-unitriangular action of determinant one. Comparing the quotient formula with right translation in the unimodular ambient group forces the conjugation factor on the actual kernel stabilizer to be exactly one. Arbitrary source additive measures and fiber families add no unproved condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR16",
      "block_sha256": "b5eba8b059ccf44755639f1094e389a6083db10f1f0b88d755446f827c1317da",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The explicit section on e,f,z preserves all pairings, and its inverse-coordinate decomposition gives a homeomorphism with S0 times the actual upper-unitriangular quotient. Triangular coordinate translations preserve the literal self-dual additive measure for the group law."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR17",
      "block_sha256": "ff1e68a9198fc59fa99d3ea8f519d6102755e2d269a35cf2a97f2162edf497ce",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The product pushforward is Haar by the established conjugation invariance, right invariance of the kernel Haar and upper-unitriangular invariance. Pointwise independence of the section preserves the original IsProdU formula without an extra measurable-section premise."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR18",
      "block_sha256": "5e68918039d1430d63bbab92c66bf39871b2fa467cd2fe2b6a98057580396436",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "All three LocTieW fields use the actual S0, S, omAt and sdE, at every original finite place and supplied ambient Haar. The original frame/rank/character premises are retained and the r=0 branch has mass one."
    },
    {
      "id": "GMR19",
      "block_sha256": "72e3a60d1005f7098e9cc9d8ea5b5a276c907cf14f49da3665c5b5efb65fa222",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The rank inequalities and standard-frame Gram determinant are checked on the supplied setting. One character precedes every word, place and auxiliary tuple. AMD17 preserves both infinity measures, the prescribed global H measure and all local S measures. Only the permitted measure entries change; all five MeasTie clauses, MeasCompat and every LocCompat are supplied. Forms0, transport, arithmetic volumes, counts and GLOBAL_SPECTRAL remain separate."
    }
